1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,080
Nose picking is a habit far more people share than you'd guess — most adults do it occasionally, and some do it several times a day without even noticing.

2
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:13,920
It feels harmless, but it can open the door to infections that are easy to avoid once you know what's going on.

3
00:00:14,240 --> 00:00:19,360
One risk is nasal vestibulitis, a bacterial infection near the opening of your nostril.

4
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:26,000
Picking irritates and can break the skin just inside your nose, and that small injury gives bacteria an easy way in.

5
00:00:26,320 --> 00:00:30,080
The area often ends up red, swollen, and tender to the touch.

6
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:32,640
The bigger concern is Staphylococcus aureus.

7
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:43,760
A large-scale study of the nasal microbiome from the Wellcome Sanger Institute, the University of Cambridge, and Imperial College London confirmed that roughly 30 percent of people carry S.

8
00:00:44,080 --> 00:00:46,720
aureus in their nose without any symptoms at all.

9
00:00:47,040 --> 00:00:49,680
It's harmless there — until it gets into a wound.

10
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:56,400
If a scratch from picking lets it into deeper tissue, it can cause a painful infection that sometimes needs medical treatment.

11
00:00:56,720 --> 00:00:58,560
So why does the urge keep coming back?

12
00:00:58,880 --> 00:01:00,000
Usually it's dryness.

13
00:01:00,320 --> 00:01:10,080
When the nasal lining dries out, mucus hardens and that trapped, crusty feeling makes you want to dig it out — which just irritates the lining further and restarts the cycle.

14
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:12,320
A saline spray is the easiest fix.

15
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:20,480
Rinsing or misting with saline loosens dried mucus without any decongestant ingredients, so it's safe to use as often as you need.

16
00:01:20,800 --> 00:01:33,440
Keeping indoor humidity between 40 and 60 percent — especially in air-conditioned or heated rooms — also keeps the lining from drying out in the first place, and a thin layer of petroleum jelly just inside the nostrils can help overnight.

17
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:40,640
If allergies or a lingering cold are behind the congestion, treating that underlying cause cuts down the urge more than anything else.

18
00:01:40,960 --> 00:01:53,920
And if you do need to clear something out, wash your hands first and use a tissue instead of a bare finger — one hand alone can carry tens of thousands of bacteria, so that one step keeps a bit of dryness from turning into an infection.

19
00:01:54,240 --> 00:01:58,960
See a doctor if the area stays swollen, red, or painful for more than a couple of days.
